Fix compilation with C++23.

P2321R2 adds a pair<> constructor taking a non-const reference.
In that case, when we contruct a pair involving OpaqueDataBlock
from a non-const pair, then the move constructor can be called
instead of the copy constructor, with OBJECT=OpaqueDataBlock&.
Since that's a reference type, the new expression then won't compile.
Fix by adding an OpaqueDataBlock ctor taking a non-const reference.
